# Netlify publishes the repo root ("publish = ." in netlify.toml), which means
# every file in the project is reachable over HTTP — including the database
# schema and migrations. RLS is enforced server-side so this grants nobody
# access, but there is no reason to hand out the table shapes and security
# policies to anyone who guesses the path. robots.txt only asks crawlers not
# to look; this actually refuses.
# The trailing "!" is load-bearing. Netlify only consults these rules when
# NO file exists at the requested path, so an unforced rule never fires for
# a real file like supabase/analytics.sql -- which is exactly the case we
# are trying to block. "404!" forces the rule to win over the static file.
/supabase/*    /index.html   404!

# The demo harness (dev/seed.js, dev/fake-supabase.js) exists so features that
# need years of history can be built before the beta has any. It must never be
# reachable on the live site: it replaces the Supabase client wholesale, so a
# page that loaded it would show invented meals as if they were real. Blocked
# here as well as never being referenced by any page.
/dev/*         /index.html   404!
